[Objective]:

Using the Root directory, invoke the absolute path for the command `run` which is stored in challenge, which is in turn stored in root.

[Key Concept]:

The Root is defined by `/` and invoking, say for instance, a program stored in root named `test`; executed by running `/test` that would be called invoking at the absolute path. You can keep going into any directory, as long as your huge, or small, file path starts with `/` then its an absolute path 

[Solution]:

Simply invoke the `run` command by the absolute root: `/challenge/run`

[# Relevant command(s) or code]:

`/` is the root. (If started with root, subsequent following path names would be called by absolute path, adding on this is not limited to the first directory after root it expands indefinetly.

[What I Learned]:

`/` is the root and running a path from the root is considered an absolute path. Absolute paths expand indefinetly not just to the first directory after root.

